                <pb facs="0328" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg234"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">annex</hi>.</head>
                <p>In an official letter under date the 23d June, 1887, the Chinese Government takes
                    the engagement to adjourn the nomination of consuls in the principal cities of
                    Tong-king until such date as France and China may consider that circumstances
                    permit their establishment.</p>
                <p>It is understood, moreover, that when the Chinese Government will establish
                    consuls at Hanoi and Haiphong, the French Government may appoint like officers
                    in the capitals of the provinces of Yunnan and Kuang-si.</p>
                <p>(True translation from French text.—<hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W.
                        Rockhill.</hi>)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
